# Always ship via PR

When finishing a chunk of work that changes the repo:

1. Create a `cursor/<short-desc>` branch if not already on one (never commit straight to `main`).
2. Commit the relevant changes (do not ask whether to commit).
3. Push the branch and open a PR with `gh pr create` (or push to update an existing PR for the same work).
4. Return the PR URL.

Do not wait for the user to say "commit" or "open a PR". Exceptions: secrets/credentials must never be committed; stop and report if the hard-stop guardrails in `AGENTS.md` apply.
